gyb/* linguist-vendored

# Data files are LF, on every machine.
#
# testapp/issues.csv arrived with CRLF -- the only tracked file in the repo that
# had it -- and the damage was not the line endings themselves. Any tool that
# writes the file correctly normalises them, so a one-field edit came back as a
# 183-line diff, and that diff is unreviewable: the one change that matters is
# hidden among 182 that do not. The rule is here so the next file written from
# the Windows side cannot reintroduce it.
*.csv text eol=lf

# `*.csv` does not match `*.csv2`, and .csv2 is the format this project actually
# writes. The rule above was added to stop exactly what then happened anyway:
# matrix_coverage/results.csv2 spent 2026-09-08 alternating between CRLF and LF
# from one commit to the next -- 68d46faa LF, bb7eac21 CRLF, 543815c0 LF,
# f9534bc6 CRLF -- so a merge of a two-row append arrived as a 641-line
# rewrite on both sides at once. `git check-attr eol -- matrix_coverage/results.csv2`
# reported `unspecified` while the same query on testapp/issues.csv reported
# `lf`, which is the whole story: the guard was written for the wrong glob.
#
# There are five tracked .csv2 files and none of them was covered.
#
# `*.csv` 匹配不到 `*.csv2`，而 .csv2 才是本專案實際會寫出的格式。上面那條規則正是為了阻止
# 隨後依然發生的事：matrix_coverage/results.csv2 在 2026-09-08 這天於各 commit 之間反覆在
# CRLF 與 LF 之間跳動，於是一次「追加兩列」的合併，在兩邊同時呈現為 641 行的整檔重寫。
# `git check-attr eol` 對 results.csv2 回報 `unspecified`，對 testapp/issues.csv 回報 `lf`
# ——這就是全部的原因：守衛寫在了錯的 glob 上。當時共有五個被追蹤的 .csv2 檔，無一被涵蓋。
*.csv2 text eol=lf

# Append-only logs merge by union, so two machines appending never conflict.
#
# BOTH SIDES WROTE THIS RULE IN THE SAME ROUND, 2026-09-09, and the merged text
# below keeps each half's evidence because the two halves check DIFFERENT things
# and either alone would have been an unsafe rule. That is worth more than the
# rule itself: the macOS side established WHY union is safe, and the Windows side
# established WHY nothing set-like may be substituted for it.
#
# These files are written by both machines and only ever appended to. Git has no
# append-aware merge for CSV, so every merge where both recorded a run came back
# as a conflict -- five in a row before this line, each resolved by hand.
#
# **Union is safe because every record is exactly one physical line.** Checked
# rather than assumed, and checked for EVERY tracked .csv2 rather than for the
# one that hurt, which is what justifies the wide glob:
#
#     buildtime/buildtime.csv2                 37 records, 39 lines
#     matrix_coverage/coverage-matrix.csv2    111 records, 113 lines
#     matrix_coverage/executable-size.csv2     49 records, 51 lines
#     matrix_coverage/results.csv2            706 records, 708 lines
#     mistakes/mistakes.csv2                  112 records, 114 lines
#     testapp/P52-buttonstyle-findings.csv2      9 records, 11 lines
#
# Two header rows each, so records + 2 == lines means no record contains an
# embedded newline. Union merges LINE BY LINE, so a quoted field holding a
# newline would be split and interleaved: the rows either side of the join would
# each become half a row, and nothing would report it. **If a note ever needs a
# line break, this attribute has to go before that note lands.** mistakes.csv2
# is the one to watch -- its fields are prose.
#
# Re-derive, per file:
#     recs=$(csv2 -r -i FILE | wc -l); lines=$(wc -l < FILE)
#     # safe when lines == recs + 2
#
# **It must NOT be `merge=ours`, and it must NOT be a set union.** These files
# contain deliberate duplicate rows -- the same app measured twice on the same
# day is two observations, not one fact recorded twice -- and anything that
# deduplicates loses the second silently. Measured 2026-09-09: results.csv2
# holds 706 data rows of which **98 are exact duplicates of another row**. A
# set-based resolution would delete 98 measurements and report success. That was
# the trap when the 2026-09-09 conflict was resolved by hand; a set-based
# resolution dropped two rows, and the counts (685 + 3 + 2 = 690) are what
# caught it.
#
# Re-derive:
#     csv2 -r -i matrix_coverage/results.csv2 | sort | uniq -d | wc -l
#
# KNOWN LIMIT, and it fails loudly rather than silently: union merges the header
# rows too, so two sides editing a .csv2 header in the same round produce
# duplicated headers -- and csv2 validates the header count and refuses the file,
# so it surfaces as a hard error on the next read rather than as quiet
# corruption. Both sides appending data never touches the header.
#
# 只做附加的紀錄檔採 union 合併,讓兩台機器各自附加時永遠不會衝突。
#
# **兩側在 2026-09-09 的同一輪各自寫下了這條規則**,而下方合併後的文字保留了雙方的證據,因為兩者查的
# 是**不同的事**,任何一方單獨存在都會是一條不安全的規則。這件事本身比規則更值得記:macOS 側確立了
# union **為何安全**,Windows 側確立了**為何不可以拿任何集合式的做法替代它**。
#
# 這些檔案由兩台機器共同寫入,且只會被附加。Git 對 CSV 沒有「理解附加」的合併方式,因此每一次「兩台
# 機器都記錄了執行結果」的合併都會變成衝突——在這一行之前連續五次,每一次都是手工解的。
#
# **union 之所以安全,是因為每一筆記錄恰好是一個實體行。** 這是查證過的、不是假設的,而且是對**每一個**
# 被追蹤的 .csv2 都查(而非只查那個出過事的),那正是採用較寬 glob 的正當理由——各檔的記錄數與行數見
# 上表。每個檔各有兩列標頭,因此「記錄數 + 2 == 行數」即代表沒有任何記錄內含換行。union 是**逐行**
# 合併的,因此一個「引號內含換行」的欄位會被拆開並交錯:接縫兩側的列會各自變成半列,而且沒有任何東西
# 會回報這件事。**若日後某則備註需要換行,這條屬性必須在那則備註落地之前移除。** 要盯的是
# mistakes.csv2——它的欄位是散文。
#
# **它不可以是 `merge=ours`,也不可以是集合式的聯集。** 這些檔案含有刻意重複的列——同一支 app 在同一天
# 被量測兩次是**兩筆**觀測,不是同一個事實被記了兩遍——而任何會去重的做法都會靜默地失去第二筆。
# 2026-09-09 實測:results.csv2 有 706 個資料列,其中 **98 列與另一列完全相同**。以集合為基礎的解法
# 會刪掉 98 筆量測並回報成功。2026-09-09 那次手工解衝突時正是這個陷阱:集合式的解法掉了兩列,而是
# 那組數字(685 + 3 + 2 = 690)抓到了它。
#
# 已知限制,而且它會大聲失敗、不會靜默損壞:union 連標頭列也會合併,因此若兩側在同一輪都改了某個
# .csv2 的標頭,結果會有重複的標頭——而 csv2 會驗證標頭數量並拒絕該檔,所以那會在下一次讀取時以硬性
# 錯誤出現,而不是變成無聲的損壞。兩側都只是附加資料時,根本不會碰到標頭。
*.csv2 merge=union
